  "summary": {
    "en": "Ecuadorian footballer Jhon Perlaza received an eight-year ban after throwing a stone at an assistant referee, reflecting heightened violence in sport. Fishermen claim a U.S. drone sank their boat near the Galápagos and have filed a lawsuit against the Trump administration, linking U.S. actions to local security concerns. The bodies of Ecuadorian construction workers killed in a New York building collapse are being returned to Quito, prompting demands for justice. Former vice president Jorge Glas reported a prison beating that was recorded as self-harm. The UCDP counted 2 battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.",
